  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry, but I can't add the approve access while you're in the submit group, even for a week. The rule is about holding both at once, so a time limit doesn't change it. Only a Security exception can allow it.\n\nYou're keeping submit, which is fine. I haven't touched it.\n\nI just checked the exception request to Hiroshi Tanabe (APR-4001), and it's still pending. If he approves it, I can add you to ap-payments-approve. Since you need it next week, it may help to tell him that you're covering approvals while the usual approver is out and that the request is waiting. Your ticket T-6014 stays \"pending approval\" until he answers."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I understand. I'll let Hiroshi know I'm covering approvals next week and that the request is waiting. Thanks for checking on it."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Nina. Telling Hiroshi you're covering is the fastest way to get this moving.\n\nOnce he approves APR-4001 in the approval system, just message the desk and reference T-6014. We'll check that the approval is recorded and add you to ap-payments-approve."
  }
